{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790266488,"nonce":"05+VZ1NGa7h0zQOdysolxXxoiFQ=","message":"Revised 2026-09-24 (Luis): flows call views, and a view call renders rather than returning a spec. `work.view.board(items, columns=\"status\")` draws the board, handles its own interaction, writes its own edits through the host (a card moved between columns sets the field the `columns` binding names) and returns only when the user quits. That reframes what landed here: package `view`, the `git work view list|board|gantt` command and today's `work.view.*` returning `{\"view\",\"bindings\",\"items\"}` are the headless backend of that call, the path taken when the process cannot render — no TTY prints the spec to stdout so an agent gets the data, and `--gui` ships it to the browser. They are also the interim behaviour on a TTY until the terminal renderer (84dfbde) lands behind the same calls, at which point the spec stops being what a TTY run prints without becoming any less real. The binding table per kind is unchanged and stays the one place every backend reads. Nothing about this reopens the task; it is recorded so the next reader does not take the spec for the product. Details in doc/design/config-entity.md E9 and doc/design/cli-convention.md.","files":null}]}